msgid "Costmodel 端到端示例"
msgstr "End-to-End Example of Cost Model"

msgid "本示例展示 costmodel 后端的基本调用流程："
msgstr ""
"This example demonstrates the basic calling flow of the costmodel backend."

msgid "使用 Triton 前端算子生成 TTIR；"
msgstr "Use the Triton frontend operator to generate TTIR."

msgid "为多个候选 config 构造 `costmodel_bench` item；"
msgstr ""
"Construct `costmodel_bench` items for multiple candidate configurations;"

msgid "对每个 item 调用一次 `costmodel_bench`，并汇总每个 config 的预测耗时。"
msgstr ""
"Call `costmodel_bench` once for each item, and aggregate the predicted "
"latency of each config."

msgid ""
"这个流程适合在 autotune 前快速筛掉预计性能较差的 config。示例只使用向量加法 kernel，便于聚焦 costmodel "
"的输入和返回值。"
msgstr ""
"This process is suitable for quickly filtering out configs with expected "
"poor performance before autotune. The example only uses a vector addition "
"kernel to focus on the inputs and return values of the costmodel."

msgid "完整示例"
msgstr "Complete example"

msgid "将下面的代码保存为 `costmodel_example.py` 后运行："
msgstr "Save the following code as `costmodel_example.py` and run it:"

msgid ""
"from __future__ import annotations\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"from triton.backends.ascend.runtime.costmodel_runtime import costmodel_bench\n"
"from triton.backends.compiler import GPUTarget\n"
"from triton.compiler import ASTSource\n"
"from triton.compiler.code_generator import ast_to_ttir\n"
"from triton.compiler.compiler import make_backend\n"
"from triton._C.libtriton import ir\n"
"from triton._C.libtriton.ascend import ir as ascend_ir\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, output_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n"
"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    mask = offsets < n_elements\n"
"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, x + y, mask=mask)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def make_ttir(kernel, signature, constants):\n"
"    source = ASTSource(kernel, signature, constants, attrs=None)\n"
"    target = GPUTarget(\"npu\", \"\", 32)\n"
"    backend = make_backend(target)\n"
"\n"
"    options = backend.parse_options(\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"num_warps\": 8,\n"
"            \"num_stages\": 2,\n"
"            \"debug\": False,\n"
"            \"multibuffer\": False,\n"
"            \"compile_mode\": \"simd\",\n"
"            **source.parse_options(),\n"
"        }\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"    context = ir.context()\n"
"    ir.load_dialects(context)\n"
"    ascend_ir.load_dialects(context)\n"
"    return str(ast_to_ttir(kernel, source, context, options, {}, {}))\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"signature = {\n"
"    \"x_ptr\": \"*fp32\",\n"
"    \"y_ptr\": \"*fp32\",\n"
"    \"output_ptr\": \"*fp32\",\n"
"    \"n_elements\": \"i32\",\n"
"}\n"
"n_elements = 98432\n"
"configs = [\n"
"    {\"name\": \"block256\", \"BLOCK_SIZE\": 256},\n"
"    {\"name\": \"block1024\", \"BLOCK_SIZE\": 1024},\n"
"    {\"name\": \"block2048\", \"BLOCK_SIZE\": 2048},\n"
"]\n"
"\n"
"items = []\n"
"for cfg in configs:\n"
"    ttir = make_ttir(add_kernel, signature, {\"BLOCK_SIZE\": cfg[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"]})\n"
"    items.append(\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"config\": cfg[\"name\"],\n"
"            \"ttir\": ttir,\n"
"            # n_elements is the 4th argument in the signature, corresponding to %arg3 in TTIR.\n"
"            # pid_x provides a static estimated value for tl.program_id(0).\n"
"            \"arg_bindings\": f\"arg3={n_elements},pid_x=0\",\n"
"        }\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"latencies = {}\n"
"for item in items:\n"
"    config, latency_us = costmodel_bench(item)\n"
"    if config is not None:\n"
"        latencies[config] = latency_us\n"
"\n"
"for config, latency_us in sorted(latencies.items(), key=lambda item: item[1]):\n"
"    print(f\"{config}: {latency_us:.3f} us\")"
msgstr ""
"from __future__ import annotations\n"
"\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"from triton.backends.ascend.runtime.costmodel_runtime import costmodel_bench\n"
"from triton.backends.compiler import GPUTarget\n"
"from triton.compiler import ASTSource\n"
"from triton.compiler.code_generator import ast_to_ttir\n"
"from triton.compiler.compiler import make_backend\n"
"from triton._C.libtriton import ir\n"
"from triton._C.libtriton.ascend import ir as ascend_ir\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, output_ptr, n_elements, BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr):\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)\n"
"    offsets = pid * BLOCK_SIZE + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    mask = offsets < n_elements\n"
"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, x + y, mask=mask)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def make_ttir(kernel, signature, constants):\n"
"    source = ASTSource(kernel, signature, constants, attrs=None)\n"
"    target = GPUTarget(\"npu\", \"\", 32)\n"
"    backend = make_backend(target)\n"
"\n"
"    options = backend.parse_options(\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"num_warps\": 8,\n"
"            \"num_stages\": 2,\n"
"            \"debug\": False,\n"
"            \"multibuffer\": False,\n"
"            \"compile_mode\": \"simd\",\n"
"            **source.parse_options(),\n"
"        }\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"    context = ir.context()\n"
"    ir.load_dialects(context)\n"
"    ascend_ir.load_dialects(context)\n"
"    return str(ast_to_ttir(kernel, source, context, options, {}, {}))\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"signature = {\n"
"    \"x_ptr\": \"*fp32\",\n"
"    \"y_ptr\": \"*fp32\",\n"
"    \"output_ptr\": \"*fp32\",\n"
"    \"n_elements\": \"i32\",\n"
"}\n"
"n_elements = 98432\n"
"configs = [\n"
"    {\"name\": \"block256\", \"BLOCK_SIZE\": 256},\n"
"    {\"name\": \"block1024\", \"BLOCK_SIZE\": 1024},\n"
"    {\"name\": \"block2048\", \"BLOCK_SIZE\": 2048},\n"
"]\n"
"\n"
"items = []\n"
"for cfg in configs:\n"
"    ttir = make_ttir(add_kernel, signature, {\"BLOCK_SIZE\": cfg[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"]})\n"
"    items.append(\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"config\": cfg[\"name\"],\n"
"            \"ttir\": ttir,\n"
"            # n_elements is the 4th argument in the signature, corresponding to %arg3 in TTIR.\n"
"            # pid_x provides a static estimated value for tl.program_id(0).\n"
"            \"arg_bindings\": f\"arg3={n_elements},pid_x=0\",\n"
"        }\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"latencies = {}\n"
"for item in items:\n"
"    config, latency_us = costmodel_bench(item)\n"
"    if config is not None:\n"
"        latencies[config] = latency_us\n"
"\n"
"for config, latency_us in sorted(latencies.items(), key=lambda item: item[1]):\n"
"    print(f\"{config}: {latency_us:.3f} us\")"

msgid "示例输出"
msgstr "Example output"

msgid "不同版本的 costmodel 参数可能会使具体数值略有不同，但输出结构类似："
msgstr ""
"Cost model parameters in different versions may cause slight variations in "
"specific values, but the output structure is similar:"

msgid ""
"block256: 0.098 us\n"
"block1024: 0.110 us\n"
"block2048: 0.126 us\n"
msgstr ""
"block256: 0.098 us\n"
"block1024: 0.110 us\n"
"block2048: 0.126 us\n"

msgid ""
"`costmodel_bench` 每次评估一个 item，返回 `(config, latency_us)`。上层 autotune "
"逻辑可以逐个调用并汇总成字典，再按预测耗时排序，优先保留预测更快的 config。"
msgstr ""
"`costmodel_bench` evaluates one item at a time and returns `(config, "
"latency_us)`. The upper-layer autotune logic can call it for each item and "
"aggregate the results into a dictionary. It then sorts the results by "
"predicted latency and retains the faster predicted configs first."

msgid "关键点说明"
msgstr "Key Points Explanation"

msgid "`ASTSource + ast_to_ttir` 只生成 TTIR，不会真实编译或启动 kernel。"
msgstr ""
"`ASTSource + ast_to_ttir` only generates TTIR and does not actually compile "
"or launch the kernel."

msgid ""
"`config` 会影响 `tl.constexpr`，例如 `BLOCK_SIZE`，因此每个候选 config 都需要生成各自的 TTIR。"
msgstr ""
"`config` affects `tl.constexpr`, such as `BLOCK_SIZE`, so each candidate "
"config requires generating its own TTIR."

msgid ""
"`costmodel_bench` 每次只接收一个 item。该 item 至少包含 `config` 和 `ttir`，也可以附带 "
"`arg_bindings`。"
msgstr ""
"`costmodel_bench` accepts only one item at a time. This item contains at "
"least `config` and `ttir`, and may also include `arg_bindings`."

msgid ""
"`arg_bindings` 用于把运行时整数参数绑定到 TTIR 中的 `%argN`。例如本例中 `n_elements=98432` 对应 "
"`arg3=98432`。"
msgstr ""
"`arg_bindings` is used to bind runtime integer parameters to `%argN` in "
"TTIR. For example, in this case, `n_elements=98432` corresponds to "
"`arg3=98432`."

msgid ""
"如果 kernel 中使用 `tl.program_id(0)`，通常需要传入 `pid_x=0`。如果还使用 "
"`tl.num_programs(0)`，可额外传入 `num_programs_x=...`。"
msgstr ""
"If the kernel uses `tl.program_id(0)`, you typically need to pass `pid_x=0`."
" If it also uses `tl.num_programs(0)`, you can additionally pass "
"`num_programs_x=...`."
